«
@@ ============================================================
@@ Elongation — Sun-Earth-planet angle (elongation) of a planet
@@ Editable AstroExamples entry, companion of LightTime.
@@ Type 1-7 (or 0 to quit), ENTER to push it, then = to run. Computes today's
@@ elongation: the angle Sun-Earth-planet, i.e. how far the planet sits from the
@@ Sun in our sky. Small = near the Sun (hard to see); large = well placed.
@@ Displays it and leaves Target/Elongation tagged on the stack.
@@ An invitation to build your own RPL program from the astronomy library.
@@ Author & design         : Jean Wilson
@@ Co-authors & programming : Claude & Claude Code (Anthropic)
@@ ============================================================
  DEPTH → d0
  «
    CLLCD
    "  Elongation of a planet" 1 DISP
    "1 Mercury  2 Venus  3 Mars" 3 DISP
    "4 Jupiter  5 Saturn" 4 DISP
    "6 Uranus   7 Neptune" 5 DISP
    "0 = Quit" 6 DISP
    "Pick, ENTER, then =" 7 DISP
    HALT
    IF DEPTH d0 > THEN
      → n
      «
        IF n 0 ≠ THEN
          IF n 1 ≥ n 7 ≤ AND THEN
            DEG
            DateTime JDN → jd
            «
              jd Ⓛ♁Pf → E
              «
                jd { 'Ⓛ☿Φf' 'Ⓛ♀Φf' 'Ⓛ♂Φf' 'Ⓛ♃Φf' 'Ⓛ♄Φf' 'Ⓛ⛢Φf' 'Ⓛ♆Φf' } n GET EVAL ⓁPosΦf → P
              «
                E NEG P E - → a b
                «
                  a b DOT a a DOT √ b b DOT √ · / ACOS → elong
                  «
                    { "Mercury" "Venus" "Mars" "Jupiter" "Saturn" "Uranus" "Neptune" } n GET → name
                    «
                      CLLCD
                      "Target: " name + 1 DISP
                      "Elongation:" 3 DISP
                      "  " elong + 4 DISP
                      "(Sun-Earth-planet angle)" 6 DISP
                      "Press any key" 7 DISP
                      -1 WAIT DROP
                      name "Target" →Tag
                      elong "Elongation" →Tag
                    »
                  »
                »
              »
              »
            »
          ELSE
            CLLCD
            "Invalid choice." 3 DISP
            "Enter 1-7, or 0 to quit." 4 DISP
            "Press any key" 6 DISP
            -1 WAIT DROP
          END
        END
      »
    END
  »
»
